==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[File:Guitar picks DSC06879.jpg|thumb|Plectra alias picks]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|plectron}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*pel- (beat)|*-trom}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|la|plēctrum}}, from {{uder|en|grc|πλῆκτρον||anything to strike with, an instrument for striking the lyre, a spear point}}, from {{m|grc|πλήσσειν||to strike, to smite, to sting}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈplɛk.tɹəm/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-plectrum.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|plectra}}

# {{lb|en|music}} A small piece of plastic, metal, ivory, etc., for [[pluck]]ing the [[string]]s of a [[guitar]], [[lyre]], [[mandolin]], etc.
# {{lb|en|anatomy|zoology}} A [[projection]] of bone or other stiff tissue, such as the ridges in some insects' [[stridulatory]] organs.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|music}} {{l|en|guitar pick}}; {{l|en|pick}}; {{l|en|plectre}} {{q|obsolete}}

